cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the project report."
title: "Calibration Is Not Enough: A Three-Level Audit of Selective Prediction for Multi-Label ECG Classification"
abstract: >-
  A reproducibility-focused audit of calibration, abstention scores and decision
  granularity for multi-label ECG triage on PTB-XL. Temperature scaling improves
  expected calibration error by 3.5x while leaving the risk-coverage curve
  essentially unchanged; the score layer has a measurable budget of 6.9 points at
  80% coverage, and decision granularity changes the achievable operating point
  more than any post-hoc score does.
